      "message": "Rather than immediately triggering the callback after requesting the change, the callbacks should originate from the callbacks that we receive from the lower layer stack (below topshim/btif). We receive such callbacks here: http://osscs/android/_/android/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/e91f5f48b01e12ee31d0339d00c07cbdc5b840f1:system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth.rs;l\u003d456;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;drc\u003d092f7c50c882e9409f927a8009595712d2dfee74\n\nThat way there is a guarantee that the callback is triggered to clients when the change actually happens and after it happens.\n\nAlso applies to discoverable changed below.",
